schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: Ithaca Hours, Bristol Pound, and Brixton Pound declined after single-steward dependency
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    Ithaca Hours (a paper local currency launched in Ithaca, NY in 1991, with
    over $100,000 in circulation at its peak) declined after founder Paul
    Glover moved away and stopped acting as the full-time promoter/
    facilitator/troubleshooter; the Bristol Pound withdrew its currency in
    2020 and its successor closed in 2023; the Brixton Pound is now paused
    for a governance transition.
  evidence: >-
    Stated in is-community-ready.md's "The One Failure Mode to Plan Around"
    section, citing the Wikipedia overview of Ithaca Hours for that case and
    asserting the Bristol/Brixton Pound outcomes without a direct citation
    for those two.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/is-community-ready.md
  interpretation: >-
    Used as the article's central cautionary pattern: a local-currency/node
    project that runs on one heroic individual has that individual as a
    single point of failure.
  uncertainty: >-
    The Ithaca Hours account traces to the article's cited Wikipedia source;
    the Bristol Pound and Brixton Pound outcomes are asserted without a
    specific citation in the source article and were not independently
    verified for this ingestion.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/is-community-ready.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
